      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Nexus-7 Optical Sensor Quick-Start Guide**\n\n**Model:** Nexus-7 Optical Sensor\n\n**Voltage:** 5V DC (regulated)\n\n**Connection:** Uses a 4-pin JST connector which includes VCC, GND, Data, and Clock.\n\n**Mounting:** The device should be mounted to flat surfaces by aligning the M3 screw holes on the corners.\n\n**Setup:**\n1. **Connections:**\n   - Attach the 4-pin JST connector: VCC (power), GND (ground), Data, Clock.\n   - Ensure secure connection avoiding loose contacts.\n\n2. **Mounting:**\n   - Use the M3 screws on the corners to mount the device on your working surface, designed for stability.\n\n3. **Initialization:**\n   - Use the Nexus Controller to connect the Sensor.\n   - Run 'sensor_init.sh' on the Nexus Controller to initialize the Sensor.\n\n4. **LED Status Check:**\n   - After initialization, a solid green LED indicates the Sensor is ready to be used.\n   - If the LED is blinking red, there is an error. Review the connection setup or calibration process.\n\n**Safety:** \n- **Calibration:** The Optical Sensor should never be exposed to direct sunlight",
